Voice sessions belong to the signed-in person:
  ✓ owner can read the session
  ✓ another account cannot read the session
  ✓ a closed session is removed before another turn
  ✓ an expired session is removed safely

Final transcript ids are held while a turn is running:
  ✓ duplicate event cannot start another turn

A voice action needs visible review and an exact phrase:
  ✓ speech alone is refused before review
  ✓ ambiguous confirmation is refused
  ✓ reviewed exact phrase can proceed to the existing Copilot action route

Ordinals only resolve an active clarification:
  ✓ Arabic الثاني selects the second active option
  ✓ a consumed clarification cannot be selected again
  ✓ Arabic الأول selects the first active option
  ✓ English third selects the third active option
  ✓ English first selects only when a choice is active
  ✓ ambiguous ordinal phrasing is not treated as a selection
  ✓ a stale clarification cannot be selected

Development evaluation fixtures are final transcripts only:
  ✓ Arabic, English-mixed, clarification, context, and follow-up fixtures are defined
  ✓ fixtures contain no audio or provider events

